      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "Given that $x$ is one-half the value of $y$, which is one-fifth the value of $z$, we can translate this statement into an equation. \n\nFirst, find the value of $y$ in terms of $z$:\n\n$y = \\frac{1}{5}z$, since $y$ is one-fifth the value of $z$.\n\nNext, find the value of $x$ in terms of $y$:\n\n$x = \\frac{1}{2}y$, since $x$ is one-half the value of $y$.\n\nFinally, find the value of $x$ in terms of $z$ by substituting the value of $y$ into the equation for $x$:\n\n$x = \\frac{1}{2}y = \\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\frac{1}{5}z\\right) = \\frac{1}{10}z$.\n\nSince $z$ is 60, we can find the value of $x$ by substituting 60 into the equation:\n\n$x = \\frac{1}{10}(60) = \\boxed{6}$.",
